- op: discuss  # c1ee
  at: '2026-11-04T17:53:16Z'  # c1ee
  by: agent  # c1ee
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c1ee
  clock: 3  # c1ee
  nonce: c1ee  # c1ee
  message: "OWNER RULING 2026-11-04: option (a). A module_completeness grant vouches for the CLASSES the module DEFINES and never for a submodule; the adjudication must distinguish a class-qualified slot from a submodule slot (scip reports the kind); every existing grant is re-read to state that its classes were enumerated; the I/O-bearing classes (io.TextIOWrapper, io.BufferedIOBase, sqlite3.dbapi2, tarfile.TarInfo, threading.Thread, ...) get real class-level rows under both options. Rationale recorded in the docs PR that follows (ADR + VERIFY-CLAIMS-SCOPE + measurement 0031). Implementation is this item, now unblocked."  # c1ee
- op: discuss  # ffbb
  at: '2026-11-04T19:13:12Z'  # ffbb
  by: agent  # ffbb
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ffbb
  clock: 4  # ffbb
  nonce: ffbb  # ffbb
  message: "Docs PR #2047 merged (dev 4c9d5d4d2f): the ruling and its rationale are ADR-0016 s7 'What a completeness grant vouches for', with the per-language oracle order (producer kind stamp; Go slash; Python stdlib list; otherwise exact), the widened meaning of complete (functions plus the methods of the types the module defines), the one-time re-read of existing grants, type-key rows for I/O-bearing types, and the pre-registered re-run. VERIFY-CLAIMS-SCOPE, CATALOGUES (generated from catalogues_doc.py), the self overlay header and measurement 0031 carry it too. This item is now the implementation: the kind stamp on the edge, the gate's type-aware match beside module_io_is_enumerated, the grant re-read, the class rows, then the scip-python re-run (the map cache was deleted 2026-11-04 with owner approval; re-index is about 11 min and 8 GB)."  # ffbb
